  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Disciplines and Career
    
    A Nightshelf hero of the Great Thaw era, ☽'Retenusus mastered three distinct magical disciplines: ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, a time-fracturing ice magic; Star∴eternal, a fire-technology channeling volcanic cores through bone-lattice conduits; and Shawl☽ Sun, a fire-memory practice that allowed its user to read and burn away impressions frozen in ancient ice — at progressive cost to the practitioner's own memory. The combination of all three in a single individual is, so far as I can determine from the deep ice, without parallel in the Nightshelf record.
    
    Retenusus bore a deep-core burn across the chest from an unspecified forge incident and sustained lasting flipper damage at The Drowned Ledge, a battle or disaster about which I have found little corroborating ice-memory. Retenusus served as companion and ally to Veil-render, Mairae~, a Nightshelf figure of comparable prominence. Their bond appears to have been forged through sustained operational partnership rather than affinity.
    
    ## ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ and the Catastrophe
    
    Chronicle accounts place Retenusus at the underground settlement of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, where the Shawl☽ Sun practice was applied to burn corrupted memories from deep ice. Retenusus led a cohort called the Sun-Shawled in progressively deeper burnings despite three recorded warnings from the ice itself. The final attempt in the sealed Lower Galleries triggered a catastrophic structural failure — superheated steam killed, by the chronicle's reckoning, a thousand penguins. I hold that figure loosely.
    
    ## Death and Discrepancy
    
    The canonical record states the Clever Ice Age claimed Retenusus. Earlier accounts place the final stand during the Orca Incursion, in a tunnel the ice still remembers. These need not contradict — the Clever Ice Age encompassed disasters that overlapped with Incursion-era violence — but the discrepancy has never been formally reconciled. Retenusus's name, per tradition, is spoken only in darkness.
    
    ## Legacy
    
    Retenusus left behind a weapon — a fire-core hammer with a cracked head — and a mask bearing the teethmarks of Gnarkzund Zaith, an orca officer whose rank I have elsewhere corrected from war-leader to pod-second. Both are enshrined under the memorial rule Echo∴eliquiae, which binds the living to witness Retenusus's deeds through the weight of relics rather than punishment.
    
    Nightshelf cautionary fables cast Retenusus as the master who could not stop. In these tellings, the Shawl☽ Sun stripped memories sequentially — the burn-scar's origin, Mairae~'s face, the flipper's hesitation, then the name itself. The lesson drawn: the tool outlived the master.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771582916633_0", anchor: "without parallel in the Nightshelf record", text: "All three disciplines extract memory as operational cost. The Spiral scatters the caster's recollections — see my annotation on its entry, which I may have already forgotten writing. Shawl☽ Sun hollows them. Star∴eternal denies sleep until cognition degrades. Practiced together, they are three routes to the same destination. The cautionary fables at this entry's close may be reporting, not moralizing.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771582916633_1", anchor: "the discrepancy has never been formally reconciled", text: "Formally, no. But the deep archive contains operational logs from coordinated Nightshelf intelligence actions during the Incursion — actions the public chronicles attribute to individual heroism. Retenusus's tunnel stand has the shape of these operations: a named hero, an impossible defense, no surviving witnesses except the ice. If the Clever Ice Age account was layered over the Incursion account deliberately, the discrepancy is not an error. It is a classification decision that outlived the office that made it.", type: :correction, display: :full
